    "description"     "[h1]Hello, Comrade![/h1]Are capitalist oil barons charging ruinous prices for fuel while your Distribution Offices happily swipe the Republic's treasury dry? Are sleepy border clerks exporting fresh Soviet steel at fire-sale kopek prices?

Rejoice! By decree of the [b]Supreme Soviet Price Control Bureau (Gosplan Division)[/b], every Distribution Office in your glorious Republic can now be issued strict ruble and dollar orders. If foreign markets try to gouge us or pay peanuts, our loyal drivers keep their engines parked until fair Socialist value returns! [i]No more funding bourgeois yachts out of the Five-Year Plan.[/i]

{EDITION_HEADER}
Source code & releases: [url=https://github.com/ZydraHydra/WorkersAndResources-Modding]ZydraHydra GitHub[/url]

[b]Alpha Field Dispatch:[/b] Treat this mod as an early [b]Alpha[/b] release. It has only been inspected on modest republics so far and needs far more field testing on massive late-game maps packed with Distribution Offices and rail hubs. Back up your glorious republic's saves first and report any saboteurs (bugs) or slowdowns on GitHub!

[h1]Wait - What is a DLL Mod? (Step-by-Step Setup)[/h1]Ordinary Steam Workshop mods only add buildings or vehicles. Because [b]TradePriceLimits[/b] adds an in-game [b]F8[/b] menu and custom border rules, it needs a [b]Mod Loader[/b] alongside the game. Simply clicking Play in Steam will [b]not[/b] load DLL mods on its own.

Both [b]TesmioLoader (v0.4.5+)[/b] and [b]Republic Mod Loader (v1.0.1)[/b] automatically find subscribed Steam Workshop DLL mods - [b]no manual file copying required[/b]:

[b]Option A - TesmioLoader (Recommended - Mature & Updated for WRSR 1.2.0.8):[/b]
[list=1]
[*] Subscribe to this mod ([b]TradePriceLimits[/b]) - Workshop ID [i]{PUBLISHED_FILE_ID}[/i].
[*] Download & extract [url=https://github.com/MaxLegend/TesmioLoader/releases]TesmioLoader (v0.4.5+)[/url] into your WRSR game directory ([url=https://maxlegend.github.io/TesmioLoaderDocs/#/getting-started]Docs[/url]).
[*] Run [b]tesmiolauncher.exe[/b]. Since v0.4, TesmioLoader automatically scans your Steam Workshop folder and lists subscribed DLL plugins (if your Workshop is in a separate Steam library, set it in the launcher / [i]workshop_path[/i]).
[*] Tick [b]TradePriceLimits[/b], launch WRSR, and press [b]F8[/b] in-game!
[/list]
[b]Option B - Republic Mod Loader (RML - All-on-Steam Alternative):[/b]
[list=1]
[*] Subscribe to this mod ([b]TradePriceLimits[/b]) - Workshop ID [i]{PUBLISHED_FILE_ID}[/i].
[*] Also subscribe to [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3787969749]Republic Mod Loader (RML)[/url] ([url=https://github.com/Ultimate-Universe/WRSR-RepublicModLoader]GitHub[/url]).
[*] Open RML from Steam Workshop:
[code]<Your Steam Library>\steamapps\workshop\content\784150\3787969749\RepublicModLoader.exe[/code]
(Tip: create a Desktop shortcut or add it to Steam as a Non-Steam Game.)
[*] Tick [b]TradePriceLimits[/b] in RML and click [b]Launch WRSR[/b], then press [b]F8[/b] in-game!
[/list]
(Manual/Non-Steam only: this Workshop item's DLL lives at [code]<Your Steam Library>\steamapps\workshop\content\784150\{PUBLISHED_FILE_ID}\plugins\TradePriceLimits.dll[/code] -> copy into [code]<Game Dir>\plugins\[/code] if you aren't using Steam Workshop scanning.)

[h1]Operating the Price Control Terminal (In-Game)[/h1][list]
[*] Press [b]F8[/b] anytime in-game to open or close the window (or [b]Esc[/b] to close).
[*] [b]Fixed Mode (exact prices):[/b] Set a [b]Max Buy[/b] cap (blocks imports above your cap) or a [b]Min Sell[/b] floor (blocks exports below your floor). Set [b]0[/b] to leave a good unrestricted. Example: setting [i]Max Buy RUB = 45[/i] on Fuel keeps Soviet Customs fuel imports parked whenever fuel rises above 45 RUB/t.
[*] [b]Base % Mode (survives decades of inflation):[/b] Click [b]Fixed[/b] on a row to switch to [b]Base %[/b]. It snapshots today's market prices as 100%, so e.g. [i]115% Max Buy[/i] allows up to +15% above baseline and [i]85% Min Sell[/i] pauses exports if prices sink >15%.
[*] [b]Trash & Waste (negative prices):[/b] Customs pays you to import waste (shown as negative prices). Signed limits work directly - e.g. [i]Max Buy = -300[/i] means only import waste if the border pays at least 300/t.
[*] [b]Emergency Override:[/b] Citizens freezing and you need an urgent delivery at any cost? Uncheck [b]Enforce Limits[/b] at the top to suspend all rules in one click without wiping your table.
[/list]
[h1]Practical Examples (Comrade's Playbook)[/h1][list]
[*] [b]Buy the Dip, Sell the Peak (Price Guard):[/b] Set [i]Max Buy RUB = 45[/i] on Fuel so your DO only buys Soviet fuel at 45 RUB/t or less, or [i]Min Sell USD = 140[/i] on Steel so exports hold in storage until NATO pays at least 140 USD/t.
[*] [b]Get Paid to Take Waste (Negative Prices):[/b] Set [i]Max Buy USD = -280[/i] on Toxic Waste so your DO only imports it when NATO pays you at least 280 USD/t (-290 is allowed; -200 is blocked). Process or incinerate it locally to profit twice.
[*] [b]Controlled RUB <-> USD Currency Exchange (Arbitrage):[/b] Short on Dollars with Rubles to spare (or vice versa)? Pair two DOs with a buffer warehouse: DO 1 imports a high-spread good like Clothes ([i]Max Buy RUB = 500[/i]) and DO 2 exports it to NATO ([i]Min Sell USD = 640[/i]). If the spread closes, both DOs pause automatically.
[*] [b]Cross-Border Factory Margin:[/b] Buy cheap inputs on one border ([i]Max Buy RUB = 135[/i] on Fabric) and sell finished goods on the stronger border ([i]Min Sell USD = 650[/i] on Clothes).
[*] [b]Priority / Fallback Export Switching:[/b] While the mod checks RUB and USD independently (no live cross-currency comparison), you can still auto-switch borders using staggered DO storage thresholds: set DO 1 (Preferred, e.g. NATO) to export at >20% warehouse full with [i]Min Sell USD = 145[/i], and DO 2 (Backup, e.g. Soviet) at >60% full with [i]Min Sell RUB = 115[/i]. When NATO's price drops, DO 1 pauses, stock fills to 60%, and DO 2 automatically takes over!
[*] [b]Inflation-Proof with Base %:[/b] Press [b]Ctrl+R[/b] (Rebase) to snapshot today's prices as 100%, switch to [b]Base %[/b], and set e.g. [i]Max Buy = 95%[/i] / [i]Min Sell = 105%[/i] so your rules scale across the decades.
[/list]
[h1]Five-Year Plan Guarantees (Save-Safe & Performance)[/h1][list]
[*] [b]Convoys already rolling stay rolling:[/b] Blocking checks [b]new dispatches only[/b]. Trucks and trains already out on the road will finish their current trip safely.
[*] [b]100% Save-Safe & Rebindable Key:[/b] Rules stay inside a tiny [i]trade_price_limits.ini[/i] file per save folder (binary WRSR saves are never altered). To change the hotkey before launching, edit [i]toggle_key=F8[/i] under [i][settings][/i] in [i]TradePriceLimits.ini[/i] beside the plugin DLL (directly editable via RML's [i]Open plugin INI[/i]).
[*] [b]Separate RUB & USD limits:[/b] Police Soviet border posts (RUB) and Western customs (USD) independently.
[*] [b]Blocked Checks Readout:[/b] Live readout shows blocked Distribution Office customs evaluations since the last Save / Autosave / Load.
[/list]{CHANGELOG_SECTION}"
